    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "Indonesian-style system with Javanese numerals: 'jam loro luwih seprapat' (2:15), 'jam setengah telu' (2:30, half to three), 'jam telu kurang seprapat' (2:45). Minutes use native 'limang menit', 'rong puluh menit', 'selawé menit'. Also changed noon from 'awan' (just 'daytime') to 'tengah awan' (midday), parallel to 'tengah wengi'. Doubt: some speakers say 'setengah telu' without 'jam'; both are heard."
    }
